  "body": "  The ring is a complete uniform nonnoetherian Tate -algebra and an integral domain. Moreover,    Lean (isTateRing_JetA)  Lean (finiteJet_isUniform_of_dvr)  Lean (isPowerBounded_JetA_iff)  Lean (finiteJet_isDomain)  Lean (finiteJet_not_noetherian)   For , define This maximum exists because is -adically separated and . We claim that After multiplying and by suitable powers of , it is enough to treat the case . Their reductions are nonzero elements of This is a domain, so the product of the reductions is nonzero. This proves ; in particular, is a domain.  The support description gives Every element of is power-bounded because is a subring. Conversely, let . Then , and by , . Hence the powers of cannot all lie in any fixed . Thus is not power-bounded. It follows that , so is uniform. Completeness follows from the completeness of , and is a domain because it is a subring of .  For nonnoetherianity, let . If were generated by , then, for every , comparison of the -coefficient in an expression would express as a -linear combination of the -coefficients of the . This would make a finite -module, which is impossible: a finite algebra is integral, whereas a monic equation for , after multiplication by a power of , would put in the proper ideal . Thus is not finitely generated, and is not noetherian.   "
