  "body": " Coefficientwise localization   Let be a rational datum in , and put . There is a canonical topological algebra isomorphism It is natural for rational refinements represented in a finite head: if is the corresponding head restriction map, the induced restriction sends The same statement holds after increasing .    Let Since is affinoid, the graph ideal is closed and the graph map is strict; this is the degree-zero conclusion of . In particular, there is a constant such that every has a lift with .  By , Because the graph relations lie in the finite head, the graph differential acts coefficientwise. Its image is exactly Indeed, the inclusion from left to right is immediate. Conversely, for a null family in , choose coefficientwise lifts with ; then is again a null family. Thus the graph ideal over is closed and as complete topological modules and as algebras. Since , this proves .  Every map used in is induced by the canonical graph quotient. If a further rational datum lies in the head, its graph differential is again coefficientwise, so the same construction gives . Presentation independence and transitivity of rational localization extend this compatibility to iterated refinements and to a larger finite head.   "
